ding the seat.", "No usable general-election polls; forecast rests on fundamentals and expert ratings.", "Incumbent Russell Fry (R) is running."]}, "overview": "Russell Fry, the Republican incumbent, seeks a third term in a northeastern South Carolina district that leans about twelve points Republican at the partisan baseline. He has raised nearly $2 million, far outpacing Democrat John Vincent, a Navy veteran who has shown notable fundraising for a challenger but trails in cash and name recognition. Prediction markets give Fry roughly a 97% chance of holding the seat.\n\nThe race has drawn genuine local attention, with both candidates campaigning actively in Horry County and debating local issues like the SC 31 extension. A late Democratic-sponsored poll of likely voters showed Fry ahead by only four points, far closer than fundamentals imply, but no independent polling corroborates that. The forecast still expects a Republican win in the low double digits, with some added uncertainty from the thin and partisan polling record.", "history": [{"date": "2026-09-22", "p_dem": 0.0379, "margin": -13.69}, {"date": "2026-09-23", "p_dem": 0.0396, "margin": -14.0}, {"date": "2026-09-24", "p_dem": 0.0447, "margin": -12.0}, {"date": "2026-09-25", "p_dem": 0.0469, "margin": -12.0}, {"date": "2026-09-26", "p_dem": 0.0326, "margin": -14.0}, {"date": "2026-09-27", "p_dem": 0.0257, "margin": -14.0}, {"date": "2026-09-28", "p_dem": 0.036, "margin": -14.0}, {"date": "2026-09-29", "p_dem": 0.0238, "margin": -15.0}, {"date": "2026-09-30", "p_dem": 0.0563, "margin": -12.0}, {"date": "2026-10-01", "p_dem": 0.0259, "margin": -14.0}, {"date": "2026-10-02", "p_dem": 0.0491, "margin": -13.0}, {"date": "2026-10-03", "p_dem": 0.0232, "margin": -15.0}, {"date": "2026-10-04", "p_dem": 0.1238, "margin": -9.0}, {"date": "2026-10-05", "p_dem": 0.0107, "margin": -16.0}, {"date": "2026-10-06", "p_dem": 0.0249, "margin": -13.0}, {"date": "2026-10-07", "p_dem": 0.0394, "margin": -13.0}, {"date": "2026-